  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "Find the solutions **in degrees** to the equation $2\\operatorname{tan}\u2061x-2\\sqrt{3}=0$ for ${0}^{\u2218}\\le x<{360}^{\u2218}.$\n\n**In ascending order,** the solutions are $x=$\n{{field-1}}${}^{\u2218}$ and $x=$\n{{field-2}}${}^{\u2218}.$",
  "worked_solution": "First, we rearrange the equation and isolate $\\operatorname{tan}\u2061x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{tan}\u2061x-2\\sqrt{3} & =0 \\\\ 2\\operatorname{tan}\u2061x & =2\\sqrt{3} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}\u2061x & =\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=arctan\\,(\\sqrt{3})={60}^{\u2218}\n$$\n\nSince ${60}^{\u2218}$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}={60}^{\u2218}.$\n\nTo generate more solutions, we add integer multiples of ${180}^{\u2218}.$ Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & ={180}^{\u2218}+{x}_{1} \\\\  & ={180}^{\u2218}+{60}^{\u2218} \\\\  & ={240}^{\u2218}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, in ascending order, the solutions are $x=60\\,{\\,}^{\u2218}$ and $x=240\\,{\\,}^{\u2218}.$",
